# A literal NUL byte in a .ts file is legal source, and once one got in nothing
# noticed: lint, typecheck, build and the test suite were all green. The only
# symptom was git reclassifying the file as binary, which silently removes it from
# every diff and therefore from review. Force text diffs so that can never hide.
*.ts   diff
*.tsx  diff
*.mts  diff
*.cts  diff
*.js   diff
*.jsx  diff
*.mjs  diff
*.cjs  diff
*.json diff
*.css  diff
*.java diff
*.sql  diff
*.xml  diff
*.yml  diff
*.yaml diff
*.md   diff
*.txt  diff
.gitignore  diff
.gitattributes diff
.env.example   diff
Dockerfile* diff

# Line endings: LF in the working tree on every platform, because the formatters (Spotless, Prettier) emit LF and
# their checks would fail on a CRLF checkout (core.autocrlf=true). Windows batch files need CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
